  "note": "Election of the county council, 1946, the first after the wartime postponement of the 1942 and 1945 elections: nominations received by W. Jenkinson, returning officer, 19 September 1946; contests in Armagh and Lurgan, polled 3 October 1946. The Belfast News-Letter prints no party labels, so none are given for the unopposed members. Hawthorne, Richardson, McCreesh and Mrs. Greeves were new members. Polled 3 October 1946. Malcolm and Major J. O'B. (Hugh O'B.) Greer were the retiring members (their joint address, Lurgan Mail, 28 September 1946, p. 2)."
